Hmm, but that has two mechanisms. Simpler and fully robust: catch and treat any error as "already there" only if the path now exists:

```js
  // MEMFS reports an existing directory by throwing an errno-only error, so
  // treat "the path is now present" as success rather than parsing messages.
  function mkdir(FS, path) {
    try { FS.mkdir(path); }
    catch (error) { if (!exists(FS, path)) throw error; }
